  q: "<p>Which of the following is/are the key difference(s) between organizational change management and individual change management?</p><p>1. Organizational change management is about managing change at the process level, while individual change management is about managing change at the personal level.<br>2. Organizational change management is about implementing new technology or merging organizations, while individual change management is about addressing motivations, desires, and concerns related to the initiative.<br>3. Organizational change management is about addressing the human aspect of change, while individual change management is about addressing the technical aspect of change.</p><p>Select the correct options:</p>",
