PQ(SPG, '2023T1', 51, 1, 'mcq', { fam: "g-commpractice",
  cs: ["comm-10cs"],
  week: 2,
  diff: "moderate",
  q: "<p>You've just made a presentation to your team members about an idea you have for the company's next project. You thought you did a great job and assume that you can move forward with the implementation right away. However, a couple of your team members have come up with suggestions that would dramatically alter your course of action. What do you think is the best way to deal with their input?</p><p>1. Creating space to ask questions and give answers.<br>2. Empower them through open and honest interactions.<br>3. Demonstrate that you possess the core competencies required for the company’s next project.<br>4. Go the extra mile to put in your best and come up with a new presentation.</p><p>Select the correct answer using the options given below.</p>",
  opts: ["1 only", "1 and 2 only", "1 and 3 only", "1 and 4 only"],
  ans: 1,
  why: ["False: statement 2 also applies.", "True: create space for questions and empower through open interaction.", "False: proving competence ignores their input.", "False: redoing the presentation is not dealing with input."],
  sol: "<p>When teammates suggest changes, listen: <b>create space for questions</b> (1) and <b>empower them through open, honest interaction</b> (2). Defending yourself (3) or polishing the slides (4) does not engage their input.</p>",
  trap: "Statement 4 sounds diligent." });
