PQ(SPG, '2025T3', 219, 5, 'short', { fam: "g-sa",
  cs: ["ei-goleman"],
  week: 5,
  diff: "moderate",
  q: "<p>[When Every Word Matters: Communicating Layoffs] Drawing on Devika’s situation and the two drafts, explain how a leader’s tone and authenticity can build or erode trust and morale during high-stakes communication. Structure your analysis using Daniel Goleman’s five components of Emotional Intelligence. (Answer in about 100 words, 5 marks)</p>",
  model: "<p>Using Goleman’s five components, tone and authenticity in a layoff message build or erode trust:</p><ol><li><b>Self-awareness:</b> Devika knows her own discomfort and does not hide behind jargon.</li><li><b>Self-regulation:</b> calm, steady tone; no defensiveness or spin.</li><li><b>Motivation:</b> a credible path forward for the company and those leaving.</li><li><b>Empathy:</b> acknowledges loss and fear before the business case.</li><li><b>Social skills:</b> clear next steps, open channels for questions.</li></ol><p>A cold or evasive draft fails empathy and self-regulation and erodes morale even among retained staff; an honest, human draft preserves trust.</p>",
  trap: "Listing the five components without linking each to tone or authenticity.",
  derived: "The case text was not included in the paper provided, so this model answer uses only what the question states and the course frameworks." });
