PQ(SPG, '2026T1', 4, 5, 'short', { fam: "g-sa",
  cs: ["ei-goleman"],
  week: 5,
  diff: "moderate",
  q: "<p>[Breaking Point at StratEdge Consulting] Using five Emotional Intelligence constructs, analyze the interaction between Ritika and Arjun in the case. Explain how applying those competencies could have improved the outcome of the discussion.(Answer in about 100 words, 5 marks)</p>",
  model: "<p>Analyse the Ritika–Arjun interaction with five EI constructs, then show the better version:</p><ol><li><b>Self-awareness:</b> each should notice rising frustration before it shapes words.</li><li><b>Self-regulation:</b> pause rather than react; keep the tone neutral.</li><li><b>Motivation:</b> keep the shared goal (the client deliverable) in view.</li><li><b>Empathy:</b> Ritika asks what pressures Arjun faces; Arjun considers her accountability.</li><li><b>Social skills:</b> agree a concrete plan and how to raise problems earlier.</li></ol><p>Applied together, these turn a breaking-point argument into a problem-solving conversation.</p>",
  trap: "Naming the constructs without tying each to what happened.",
  derived: "The case text was not included in the paper provided, so this model answer uses only what the question states and the course frameworks." });
